---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import avatar from "../images/avatar.jpg";
---

<Layout content={{ title: "About" }}>
  <main class="container mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-4xl px-6 py-20 space-y-12">
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-10 lg:flex-row lg:items-center">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm shrink-0 lg:mx-0">
        <img
          src={avatar.src}
          width={avatar.width}
          height={avatar.height}
          alt="Portrait of Pilkington"
          class="w-full rounded-3xl border-4 border-slate-500 shadow-2xl"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4 rounded-3xl border border-sky-100 bg-sky-50 p-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700 shadow-sm">
        <p>
          I'm teaching myself web development one build at a time, pairing Astro with Sanity to
          understand how modern content systems come together. I recently wrapped up a round of
          Sanity platform training, and now I'm putting that knowledge to work on personal projects
          like this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          When I'm not iterating on layouts or experimenting with new integrations, you'll usually
          find me coding for fun, kayaling across calm water, or hiking the trails of northern
          Arizona. These adventures keep me curious, energized, and ready to tackle the next
          challenge on the web.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
